# tally 2.2.1 (#221, 221.C2), L §4.4: "wherever one value is needed (a print but a date's, ...), an undecided
# interval is HOLE-IMPRECISE". gap is days_between(d0, w), an interval of 4 to 6 days; an entry of a list is printed,
# so it is that hole, and the line names w (a); the plain print (b) as before. tally 2.2 printed [window(4, 6), 1]
# (the 2.2 fix review's blocking/p25_list.tally).
=== p25_list.tally
model p25l
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "fix review, blocking 1: a window that is no window of days, inside a list, prints as a window, and the line names its day."

source s "s"

input w: date

input d0: date

def gap: int = days_between(d0, w)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  d0 = 2026-03-01 "s"

ask a: [gap, 1]
ask b: gap
=== expect
a: [?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a print" (w), 1]
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
b: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a print" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
